--- field object.certificate.digest-previous
type: bin

SHA-256 digest of the preceding certificate's DER encoding, as 32 bytes.

Compare this field with `object.certificate.digest` to identify the
certificate that a renewal replaced.

--- event gxwid.certificate.renewed
tier: essential
gating: none (every completed certificate renewal is recorded)
cardinality: once per renewal

The machine's GXWI certificate was renewed for its existing key.

GXWI checks certificates at startup, every 24 hours, and on service reload.
It renews a certificate with fewer than 30 days remaining or a validity
interval outside the accepted policy. Initial creation is not renewal.

The replacement has a different fingerprint. Users who trusted the
preceding certificate need to verify and trust its replacement according
to their browser's policy. The public certificate is
`/var/state/gxwi/certificate.pem`; its fingerprint is
`/var/state/gxwi/certificate.sha256`.

Existing TLS connections continue. Subsequent connections use the
replacement certificate after handover to the network worker.

The event has no subject because gxwid renews its own certificate.

field: object.certificate.digest            required
  SHA-256 digest of the replacement certificate.
field: object.certificate.digest-previous   required
field: object.certificate.name              required
  Certificate subject, with the machine name as `CN` and `Peios` as `O`.
